[simtest] *** SIMULATOR BUILD - this log is not from hardware ***
[simtest] Purpose: check that the program's buffer logic is right -
[simtest] that the two halves of the ping-pong buffer are filled,
[simtest] handed over and processed in the right order, without a
[simtest] half being skipped, served twice or overwritten early.
[simtest] ADC and DMA are replaced by a software stand-in (sim_dma.c):
[simtest] no conversion, no DMA transfer, no interrupt. Every sample is
[simtest] synthetic: a 1 MHz sine on the measurement input, a flat 3840
[simtest] on the self-test input. The [clk]/[adc] lines below report
[simtest] register writes whose waits were skipped, not a running PLL
[simtest] or ADC. Nothing here says anything about sample rate, DMA
[simtest] bandwidth or the hardware. README: In the MPLAB X simulator
